      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name honors Hiram S. Holly, the rancher who brought 1,300 cattle to the area.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Holly%2C_Colorado",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Holly SS Ranch Barn, a stone building with rifle ports, dates to 1871 and is on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofhollyco.gov/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Holly Sugar, founded in 1905, grew so fast it expanded beyond Colorado by 1911 before merging with Imperial Sugar in 1988.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
